#: ../../source/docs/common-mro-uavcan-adapter-node.rst:5
#: 0c4f2aa9751c4f5181ebe370ab27892a
msgid "mRobotics DroneCAN Adapter Node"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mro-uavcan-adapter-node.rst:8
#: fe3a6daa77b34eca886bff2f5b38a841
msgid "The mRo CAN Node is a collaborative project with ArduPilot. It began with a desire to make CAN peripherals more standard in the drone community. Compared to other boards that have open-source hardware but closed source code, mRo CAN node is completely open. The CAN Node F303 is the version 2 of mRobotics' CAN Node, featuring more flash space."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mro-uavcan-adapter-node.rst:10
#: 454a1b4e9f58467fb4802a92c91fb6e4
msgid "With this board, you can easily utilize the ArduPilot driver library to convert ArduPilot supported GPS, I2C, and GPIO based (ie Safety Switch) peripherals to DroneCAN bus peripherals."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mro-uavcan-adapter-node.rst:15
#: 36b780415beb4ff98c7d5162bdeedf3e
msgid "mRo CAN Node uses open-source code, which utilizes the existing and proven ArduPilot DroneCAN driver library (see :ref:`DroneCAN Adapter Nodes <common-uavcan-adapter-node>` for firmware versions and capabilities). It features a  bootloader for \"over CAN\" firmware updates and an RTOS running Chibios."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mro-uavcan-adapter-node.rst:17
#: edf0ba9616964173aebc17c97b87c3df
msgid "The adapter's CAN Node ID can be set manually or automatically (Not yet supported in stable ArduPilot). The hardware design is open source, so that anyone can contribute to the CAN peripheral world with a proven CAN / MCU interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mro-uavcan-adapter-node.rst:19
#: 86b87cde77fc40aab3394cc940acad66
msgid "As delivered, it is setup to be plug-and-play as a DroneCAN GPS/Magnetometer/LED/Airspeed by simply plugging in the 6pin GH connector from any mRo or other GPS, and connecting I2C Compasses, RGB LEDs, and/or Airspeed sensors supported by ArduPilot, as desired."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mro-uavcan-adapter-node.rst:21
#: 8c4e243b833a4233a6d59dd935f3e15b
msgid "This adapter uses the \"f303-GPS\" or \"f303-Universal\" (default) firmware in https://firmware.ardupilot.org/AP_Periph. See the :ref:`SLCAN section of DroneCAN advanced setup<common-uavcan-setup-advanced>` for downloading instructions, if changes are desired or updates become available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mro-uavcan-adapter-node.rst:24
#: cecd5d86686c42c79f669e30e0dabf1f
msgid "Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mro-uavcan-adapter-node.rst:26
#: 9002ecfaadf946ddbe8a77ba8fbef121
msgid "Verify the following parameters are set on your autopilot via your ground station."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mro-uavcan-adapter-node.rst:28
#: 2a4f883f6561425692d3fac8c3dfaab3
msgid ":ref:`CAN_P1_DRIVER<CAN_P1_DRIVER>` = 1 (assuming its on the first CAN bus of the autopilot and will be using the first driver)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mro-uavcan-adapter-node.rst:29
#: 93723169ed024b119ea010521c2043e0
msgid ":ref:`CAN_D1_PROTOCOL<CAN_D1_PROTOCOL>` = 1 (DroneCAN)(assuming its the first driver)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mro-uavcan-adapter-node.rst:30
#: 40de5221c14848738601ff40e361130d
msgid ":ref:`GPS1_TYPE<GPS1_TYPE>` = 9 (DroneCAN) or if it will be the secondary GPS, set instead"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mro-uavcan-adapter-node.rst:31
#: 18fadbfe3a274acf88347ae2576887d0
msgid ":ref:`GPS2_TYPE<GPS2_TYPE>` = 9 (DroneCAN)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mro-uavcan-adapter-node.rst:32
#: 98e2eac8abfd49e78067bf3bdede5402
msgid "Reboot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mro-uavcan-adapter-node.rst:34
#: bcf934cb3d0247018601408458c935e7
msgid "Make sure the DroneCAN compass driver is not disabled. (:ref:`COMPASS_DISBLMSK<COMPASS_DISBLMSK>` bit 9 should not be set)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mro-uavcan-adapter-node.rst:36
#: 03c44a37506d42caa8ef86f19c3f5c6b
msgid "If your controller has multiple compasses attached already, you may want to set the attached compass as a higher priority than others, if it has better precision or performance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mro-uavcan-adapter-node.rst:38
#: d4de57a4c0e1489690c02b0d301bafaa
msgid "To enable an attached I2C RGB LED set:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mro-uavcan-adapter-node.rst:40
#: 6de65469e62044309176a6d913fc05e0
msgid ":ref:`NTF_LED_TYPES<NTF_LED_TYPES>` bit 5 should be set"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mro-uavcan-adapter-node.rst:42
#: 58aaac9f05f645e499d242e9d0a95384
msgid "If you want to enable an attached I2C airspeed sensor, set:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mro-uavcan-adapter-node.rst:44
#: 9ba7ebc4f0bf42a0bb6db8718bebc54e
msgid ":ref:`ARSPD_TYPE<ARSPD_TYPE>` = 8 (DroneCAN)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mro-uavcan-adapter-node.rst:46
#: f0a3e3f500b4482b8e6af3e5ba8be838
msgid "Then you must access your Adapter's CAN parameters to select Airspeed and LED type being attached to the adapter. Using Mission Planner (or :ref:`common-uavcan-gui`), go to the menu SETUP/Optional Hardware/DroneCAN/SLCan Mode CAN1/Parameters. Once the CAN Adapters parameters appear, change the following (this changes them inside the DroneCAN adapter, NOT the autopilot, allowing the adapter to use the correct driver and convert the information to DroneCAN airspeed format):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mro-uavcan-adapter-node.rst:48
#: dffa57c278234618a50f1f5ea1231ed1
msgid ":ref:`ARSPD_TYPE<ARSPD_TYPE>` = to match your sensor type: 3,for an I2C-MS5525; 1 for an MS4525DO, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mro-uavcan-adapter-node.rst:49
#: 7bcc6645072a4b158e70d8ffbff95e25
msgid ":ref:`ARSPD_USE<ARSPD_USE>` =  1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mro-uavcan-adapter-node.rst:50
#: 6c734662778045e4a266e90c1668940c
msgid ":ref:`ARSPD_BUS<ARSPD_BUS>` =  0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mro-uavcan-adapter-node.rst:52
#: 233b3e1d24ae4524915786735a34dce8
msgid "For the LED, set its :ref:`NTF_LED_TYPES<NTF_LED_TYPES>` appropriately for the attached LED."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mro-uavcan-adapter-node.rst:54
#: 107cf590a60649269c44d1eaecbfb5b2
msgid "Then reboot."
msgstr ""

